//   'pcg' (one word to one), 'pcg2d', 'pcg3d' and 'pcg4d' (two, three and
//   four words to as many, over UVec2, UVec3 and UVec4); 'hash1', 'hash2' and
//   'hash3', a lattice point under a seed; and 'toUnit' and 'toSigned', a
//   word to a float in [0, 1) or [-1, 1), exactly; 'heavySigned', a
//   heavy-tailed draw (mostly small, now and then huge) from two words.
// - Lattice noise (lattice.cone): 'value2', 'value3', 'gradient2' and
//   'gradient3', each a Noise2 or Noise3 (the value and its analytic
//   derivative), and their '...Periodic' forms, which tile every 'period'
//   cells.
// - Cellular noise (cellular.cone): 'cellular2' and 'cellular3', a Cell2 or
//   Cell3 (F1, F2, the nearest cell's id, and the vector to its point).
// - Fractal sums (fractal.cone): 'fbm2', 'fbm3', 'ridged2', 'ridged3',
//   'billow2' and 'billow3', with their derivatives; and the domain warps
//   'warp2' and 'warp3'; 'cascade2', fBm whose octaves' amplitudes are a
//   product of noise factors (a multiplicative cascade: detail in clusters),
//   the value only and on the CPU only, with 'heavySigned' not yet in
//   noise.slang.
// - Oriented stripes (phacelle.cone, under the MPL 2.0): 'phacelle2', Rune
//   Skovbo Johansen's Phacelle noise, a phase steered by a direction.
// - Families (family.cone, CPU only): 'FamilyDial', a dial's distribution
//   (a mean, a spread, its loadings on two latent numbers and on its own
//   draw, its bounds), drawn for an individual by 'draw' or read as a chance
//   by 'chance'; 'familyLatents' and 'familyUnit'. Every number is a hash of
//   (family seed, individual, dial), never a stream.
//
// Numbers are f32 and points geomath's Vec2 and Vec3. No function keeps
// state: the same seed and point give the same result, in any order, on any
// thread.
//
// DETERMINISM. Every random number comes from 32-bit integer hashing, never
// from a float hash such as fract(sin(x) * k), whose results differ between
// GPUs. The hashes, and every decision taken on them (which cell is nearest,
// its id), are bit-identical on every machine. The float arithmetic of
// value, gradient, cellular, fractal and warp noise uses additions,
// subtractions, multiplications, floor and (for F1 and F2 only) a square
// root, written in one order: the CPU (whose code conec generates for a
// generic x86-64, with no fused multiply-add) and a GPU running noise.slang
// compiled with slangc's '-fp-mode precise' (no contraction) round each alike.
// Phacelle noise uses exp, cos, sin and division, which a GPU computes to
// looser bounds, and is close, not identical. The package README has the
// rules and what the parity test measured.
//
// noise.slang (and phacelle.slang) hold the same functions for shaders,
// under the same names. The two are kept in step by hand, and the parity
// test, tests/parity.cone, checks them against each other on a GPU.
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports:
