// ======== Fractal sums: fBm, ridged and billowed; domain warp ========
//
// Each sums 'octaves' layers of gradient noise, the first at the point's own
// scale with amplitude 1, each next at 'lacunarity' times the frequency and
// 'gain' times the amplitude (2 and 0.5 are the usual). Octave i is seeded
// by hash1(i, seed), so no two octaves, and no two seeds, share a lattice.
// The sum is not divided by the total amplitude (a division is not exact on
// a GPU); with gain g < 1 it is 1 + g + g^2 + ... < 1 / (1 - g) times one
// octave's range. Each carries its derivative, by the chain rule through the
// frequencies.

