pub extern fn toSigned(h: u32) f32;

// -------- heavy-tailed draws --------
//
// Most draws small, a rare one huge: the long spit, the deep fjord. 'u' gives
// a number in [-1, 1) as toSigned does; 'coin' decides how many times it is
// multiplied by 'ratio': once for each of its low bits that is set, counted
// from bit 0 up to the first clear one, at most 'cap' times. Each step is half
// as likely as the one before, so |draw| passes ratio^k with chance about
// 2^-k: a power-law tail of index log 2 / log ratio (ratio 2 gives index 1,
// Cauchy's; ratio sqrt 2 gives 2). A ratio of 1, or a cap of 0, is toSigned.
// Only multiplications: the same bits on every machine.
pub extern fn heavySigned(u: u32, coin: u32, ratio: f32, cap: i32) f32;

